        <div class="feature-icon">01</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Live-replica backtesting</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">The backtester runs the live bot&rsquo;s own decision functions over real data, minute by minute, with partly formed higher-timeframe candles &mdash; so a backtest result is what the bot itself would have done, with no look-ahead.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">02</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Real-time data watchdog</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">Every two minutes each bot measures how old IBKR&rsquo;s newest bar is and watches for subscription errors. If the feed falls back to delayed data it sends a Discord alert and flags it on the dashboard.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">03</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Streaming bars at the open</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">The NY bot opens live-updating bar subscriptions before 9:30 instead of polling IBKR&rsquo;s historical service, which lags 1&ndash;5 minutes at the open. If a stream stalls it falls back to normal requests automatically.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">04</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Three bots, one account</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">IBKR nets every bot into one MNQ position, so each bot connects with its own client ID and manages only its own orders. The NY ICT bot&rsquo;s 11:00 close cancels only orders it placed and closes only the contracts its own fills add up to &mdash; never another bot&rsquo;s trade.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">05</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Fill-anchored brackets</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">Stops and targets are placed after the entry fills, anchored to the actual fill price, as a One-Cancels-All pair &mdash; so slippage never turns the stop into a bigger loss than planned.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">06</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Break-even management</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">The NY ICT bot moves its stop to entry on a structural lower high / higher low, a 5-minute FVG in the trade&rsquo;s path, or an MES/MNQ divergence at a session extreme. The scalper does it at +30 points.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon">07</div>
        <div class="feature-title">Live dashboard</div>
        <div class="feature-desc">A local dashboard shows each bot&rsquo;s state, positions, live open P&amp;L, distance to stop and target, data-feed status, and a combined view of the whole account.</div>
      </div>
